---
const variants = [
  {
    slug: 'stack',
    title: 'File stack',
    oneLiner:
      'Each stage is a paper sheet of the same loan file. Scrolling pins each sheet one tab below the last, so by Collect the six tabs sit piled like a real file, each tab naming the team that worked it.',
    why: 'Shows "one record" instead of saying it: the record visibly builds up. Nothing to learn; it is plain scrolling. Every stage is read in order.',
    tradeoff:
      'The longest of the three, about five screens of scroll. Six tabs need a phone at least about 640px tall; shorter screens get slimmer tabs.',
  },
  {
    slug: 'deck',
    title: 'Stage stepper (now on the main page, all widths)',
    oneLiner:
      'One stage per page in a swipe track, the next page peeking at the edge. A I–VI strip on top is both progress and jump links; previous and next sit at the bottom in thumb reach, with the next team named between them.',
    why: 'The shortest: the whole section fits one screen. Closest to the desktop panel, so it is one pattern on both sizes. Naming the next team turns each step into a hand-off.',
    tradeoff:
      'Stages II–VI sit off-screen until the visitor swipes or taps; a visitor who only scrolls sees Apply alone. Never auto-advances.',
  },
  {
    slug: 'relay',
    title: 'Hand-off rail',
    oneLiner:
      'A vertical rail of six nodes, one stage open at a time. Closed, the rows read as the chain of teams; open, a stage shows its page of the record and a button that hands it to the next team. The rail fills up to the open stage.',
    why: 'Scannable at a glance: all six stages and their teams fit on one screen while closed. Native exclusive <details>, so it works without JavaScript, and the rail progress is pure CSS.',
    tradeoff:
      'The record pages are one tap away rather than on show. Least cinematic of the three.',
  },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="Three mobile prototypes for the How Leaf works section." />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0a0a0b" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Outfit:wght@300;400;500&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <title>How Leaf works, on a phone</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="top">
      <a class="back" href="/prototypes">&larr; All prototypes</a>
      <h1>How Leaf works, on a phone</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        The section has one job: show that a single loan record moves through six stages, worked
        by a different team at each. On desktop the light record panel proves it. Below 900px the
        current page hides that panel, so phones get six words and their captions, and tapping a
        stage does nothing visible. Each prototype below brings the record back on a phone in a
        different way. B, the stage stepper, is now the main page's layout at every width,
        desktop included; the stack and rail pages show their variant below 900px only.
      </p>
    </header>

    <main>
      <ol class="grid">
        {
          variants.map((v, i) => (
            <li class="card">
              <div class="phone">
                <iframe
                  src={`/prototypes/how-it-works/${v.slug}#lifecycle`}
                  title={`${v.title}, at phone width`}
                  loading="lazy"
                  width="390"
                  height="780"
                />
              </div>
              <span class="num">{String.fromCharCode(65 + i)}</span>
              <h2>
                <a href={`/prototypes/how-it-works/${v.slug}#lifecycle`}>{v.title}</a>
              </h2>
              <p class="one">{v.oneLiner}</p>
              <dl>
                <div>
                  <dt>Why it works</dt>
                  <dd>{v.why}</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Trade-off</dt>
                  <dd>{v.tradeoff}</dd>
                </div>
              </dl>
              <a class="open" href={`/prototypes/how-it-works/${v.slug}#lifecycle`}>
                Open /prototypes/how-it-works/{v.slug} &rarr;
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :root {
    --ground: #0a0a0b;
    --surface: #121214;
    --ink: #f2f1ee;
    --muted: #a8a6a1;
    --rule: #2a2a2c;
    --accent: #c8463f;
    color-scheme: dark;
  }

  *,
  *::before,
  *::after {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  html {
    background: var(--ground);
  }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 16px;
    background: var(--ground);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: 'Outfit', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  a {
    color: inherit;
  }

  .top,
  main {
    max-width: 1300px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .top {
    padding: 32px 0 40px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .back {
    color: var(--muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .back:hover,
  .back:focus-visible {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 32px 0 12px;
    font-size: clamp(36px, 6vw, 64px);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }

  .intro {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 68ch;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 17px;
  }

  .grid {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 40px 0 64px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 40px 28px;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1320px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 410px);
      justify-content: space-between;
    }
  }

  .card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  /* Frames only where there is room; on a phone the links open the real page. */
  .phone {
    display: none;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .phone {
      display: block;
      width: 410px;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
      border: 1px solid var(--rule);
      border-radius: 28px;
      padding: 10px;
      background: #000;
    }

    .phone iframe {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      border: 0;
      border-radius: 20px;
      background: #0f0e0c;
    }
  }

  .num {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 26px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  h2 a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  h2 a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .one {
    margin: 0;
  }

  dl {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
    padding-top: 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  dt {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 13px;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: #d6d4cf;
  }

  .open {
    align-self: flex-start;
    margin-top: 4px;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 15px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--muted);
    padding-bottom: 2px;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .open:hover,
  .open:focus-visible {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    outline: none;
  }
</style>
